{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012iDQ5ojUbvixQuphv9Wf1u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the directory exists. Now let me write the complete LaTeX paper. I need to carefully structure it with all experimental results from the JSON data. Let me organize:\n\n1. Abstract\n2. Introduction\n3. Method (CSD framework)\n4. Experiments\n   - Exp 1: Multi-judge formality pairwise (LLMBar) → Table 2\n   - Exp 2: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise → Table 3, Table S1\n   - Exp 3: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity → Table 4\n   - Exp 4: Tone axis → Table 5, Table S2\n   - Exp 5: Pairwise RATE control → Table 6, Table 7\n   - Exp 6: Scaled replication → Table 8, Table S3\n   - Exp 7: Verbosity boundary → Table 9\n   - Exp 8: Register axis → Table 10\n   - Exp 9: Non-Qwen rewriter control → Table S4\n5. Conclusion\n\nNow I'll write the comprehensive paper with careful attention to the data values, starting with the title \"Causal Style Decomposition: Revealing Axis-Dependent Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison\" and building out the full structure.\n\nFor the framing, I'm positioning the measurement gap between Likert and pairwise approaches as the central finding, with the method's judge-dependent behavior as the foundation and the axis spectrum analysis as supporting evidence.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":251,"cache_read_input_tokens":41341,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":251},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7a39814-e424-4043-b57f-59835adcd45d","uuid":"106fb995-7cfb-458c-8dd3-11f9503b5c66"}
